        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Americas</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Boyacá</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">7 August 1819; the fighting lasted a little more than two hours and ended shortly after 4:30 p.m.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Casa de Teja, beside the bridge over the Teatinos River on the Camino Real, about 150 km from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogota">Bogotá</a> in the Andes, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyaca-department">Boyacá Department</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombia">Colombia</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">A Patriot army of Venezuelans, New Granadans and a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>, with Brigadier Generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-paula-santander">Francisco de Paula Santander</a> and José Antonio Anzoátegui; the Spanish III Division of the Expeditionary Army of Costa Firme under Colonel José María Barreiro</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Spanish division was effectively dismantled: 100 dead, 150 wounded and 1,600 captured, against 66 Patriot casualties. Viceroy Juan de Sámano fled Santa Fe two days later.</span></div>
        </div>
