    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Bolívar's army crossed the Andes by the Páramo de Pisba in early July 1819, won narrowly at Vargas Swamp on 25 July, and then used a feint and a night countermarch to reach <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunja">Tunja</a> ahead of the Spanish.</li><li>On the day the Spanish vanguard and rearguard were split by the Patriot advance along the Camino Real and fought separately; the Patriots lost 13 dead and 53 wounded, the Spanish 100 dead, 150 wounded and 1,600 captured.</li><li>Within days the viceroy had fled Santa Fe, and in December 1819 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a> and Venezuela were joined as the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colombia">Colombia</a> (Gran Colombia); 7 August is now a national holiday in Colombia.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Spanish had carried their three artillery pieces unassembled, so when Arthur <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sande-society">Sandes</a>'s Rifles charged the guns only one could be put together, and it fired three shots before its carriage broke.</p></aside>
    </section>

